Recruitment Admin Portal
A single-file admin dashboard for managing job applications stored in Supabase.
Hosted on GitHub Pages — no backend, no build step required.
Features
Feature
Details
🔐 Login
Supabase Auth (email + password) — only authorised admins can access
📊 Overview
Live stats: total applications, this month, packhouse count, forklift count, monthly bar chart, recent 10
👥 Applicants
Full searchable table with sort, pagination (25/page)
🔎 Filters
Packhouse experience, forklift licence, gender, race, date range
✏️ Edit
Click any row → modal view/edit all fields, save changes back to Supabase
📂 Documents
View uploaded files (ID copy, SARS, bank proof, payslip, forklift licence) directly from Supabase Storage
🗑️ Delete
Confirm-dialog protected delete
📄 PDF Export
Single applicant · selected applicants · date range · applicant type
📊 CSV Export
Full database download · filtered/active results
Setup
1. Supabase credentials
Open admin.html and replace the two config lines near the bottom of the <script> tag:
const SUPABASE_URL  = 'https://YOUR_PROJECT_ID.supabase.co';
const SUPABASE_ANON = 'YOUR_ANON_PUBLIC_KEY';
Both values are in your Supabase project under Settings → API.
2. Create an admin user
In your Supabase project go to Authentication → Users → Add user.
Create a user with an email and password. This is what you'll use to log in.
The app uses signInWithPassword — only users you create manually can log in.
3. GitHub Pages
Create a new GitHub repo (e.g. recruit-admin)
Push admin.html as the only file
Go to repo Settings → Pages
Set source to main branch, root folder
Your admin portal will be live at https://yourusername.github.io/recruit-admin/admin.html
Keep this URL private. Share it only with people who should have admin access.
